%% section: The write path and durability
%% caption: The write path
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant B as Buffer pool
    participant W as WAL
    participant D as Data files
    C->>B: UPDATE row
    B->>B: modify the page in memory — now dirty
    B->>W: append the change record
    W->>W: fsync on commit
    Note over W: durability is the WAL's fsync, not the data file write
    W-->>C: COMMIT returns
    B-->>D: checkpoint flushes dirty pages later
    Note over D: a crash replays the WAL forward from the last checkpoint
